<div class="page-header"><h1 class="page-header__title">Pilot and Pricing</h1><p class="page-header__subtitle">HelloDeploy is free during the pilot. There are no paid plans.</p></div>
<div class="card prose"><div class="card__body">
  <h2>Free active pilot</h2>
  <p>Accounts are open after email verification, and use is free within the published limits. No future price or continued free availability is promised. If that ever changes, account holders will be told by email before anything is charged.</p>
  <h2>What the free pilot includes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><%= planDefaults.maxOwnedProjects %> project and <%= planDefaults.maxRunningApps %> running app per account</li>
    <li><%= planDefaults.deploymentsPerMonth %> deployments a month</li>
    <li><%= planDefaults.memoryMb %> MB of memory and <%= planDefaults.cpuCores %> CPU per app</li>
    <li><%= planDefaults.maxCustomDomains %> custom domain and <%= planDefaults.maxRollbackReleases %> rollback releases</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The <a href="/service-limits">Service Limits</a> page has the complete list, including build time and log retention.</p>
  <h2>Availability and recovery</h2>
  <p>This is shared pilot infrastructure without a service-level agreement. The operator maintains platform recovery procedures, but HelloDeploy does not back up or administer databases used by deployed applications.</p>
  <h2>Support</h2>
  <p>Support is best-effort by email at <a href="mailto:<%= legalContactEmail %>"><%= legalContactEmail %></a>. Features, limits, and availability may change during the pilot.</p>
  <p><a href="/features">Features</a> · <a href="/status">Current service status</a> · <a href="/terms">Terms</a></p>
</div></div>
